    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the **GOLD** membership tier: an owner is `GOLD` when their household (owners sharing the same `householdId`) has 3+ members after the create; otherwise the existing SILVER/BRONZE rules still apply.\n\nThe tier is a derived field computed in the DTO mapper (never stored as a tier), and GOLD depends on household size \u2014 which needs to be known at mapping time. Following the existing `namesakeCount` precedent (a stored input the tier reads), I stored the household size on the entity and had the mapper read it. Changes:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `householdSize` (`household_size` column) field with getter/setter, mirroring `namesakeCount`.\n\n2. **`CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique.java`** \u2014 the only step that knows the household. It now stamps `householdSize` on the new owner and on every existing household member:\n   - lone owner (no existing match) \u2192 size `1`\n   - shared household \u2192 size = existing members + 1, written to all members so the whole household's tier stays consistent as it grows.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `membershipTier` expression now yields `GOLD` when `householdSize >= 3`, otherwise falls through to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `GOLD` to the `membershipTier` enum (source of the generated `MembershipTierEnum`) and updated its description.\n\n5. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `household_size` column, since tests run under `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw clean test` \u2014 the new `coreGoldForThreeMemberHousehold` acceptance test passes, and the full suite (this project's only test class) is green with 0 failures / 0 errors.",
